<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">31 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 31 July, from 768 to 1971.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/768">768 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,258 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Lombard king Desiderius installs Philip as antipope for a day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Intervening in the crisis after the death of Pope Paul I, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desiderius">Desiderius</a> seized a priest named Philip in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and had him appointed pope. Unrecognised, Philip left the same day and returned to his monastery.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desiderius">Desiderius</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/alexios-iii-angelos" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexios-iii-angelos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1201 CE <span class="tih-ago">825 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Komnenos the Fat attempts a coup against Alexios III</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With the support of the capital's populace, the plotters seized most of the Great Palace, and John Komnenos, a descendant of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/komnenian-dynasty">Komnenian dynasty</a>, was crowned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a>. Their coup against Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexios-iii-angelos">Alexios III Angelos</a> was short-lived.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexios-iii-angelos">Alexios III Angelos</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1423">1423 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">603 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An Anglo-Burgundian army defeats a Franco-Scottish force at Cravant</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At a bridge and ford over the river <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yonne-river">Yonne</a> at Cravant in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auxerre">Auxerre</a>, the English and their Burgundian allies defeated a Franco-Scottish army in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1492">1492 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Deadline passes for Jews to leave Spain under the Alhambra Decree</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The last day allowed by Ferdinand and Isabella's expulsion edict passed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s Jewish communities left or converted. Tens of thousands went into exile, founding the Sephardic diaspora.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1556">1556 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">470 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ignatius of Loyola dies in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ignatius-of-loyola">Ignatius of Loyola</a>, the Basque soldier turned founder of the Society of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a>, died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. His Spiritual Exercises and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a>' schools and missions reshaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> worldwide.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1703">1703 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">323 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Daniel Defoe stands in the pillory for seditious libel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daniel-defoe">Daniel Defoe</a> began three days in the pillory for a satirical pamphlet mocking Tory hostility to Dissenters. By tradition the crowd threw flowers instead of filth. He later wrote Robinson Crusoe.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1790">1790 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">236 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first US patent is issued to Samuel Hopkins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Samuel Hopkins received the first patent under the new US Patent Act, for an improved way of making potash. It was signed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1917">1917 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Passchendaele begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and French forces opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-passchendaele">Third Battle of Ypres</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>. Heavy rain turned the battlefield into a swamp, and months of fighting won a few miles for hundreds of thousands of casualties.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1971">1971 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">55 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 15 astronauts drive the first rover on the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Scott and James Irwin took the battery-powered Lunar Roving Vehicle on its first drive near Hadley Rille. The rover let astronauts range much farther from their lander to collect samples.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 31 July <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philip-the-good.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Philip the Good</span><span class="tp">1396–1467</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-ii-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maximilian-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maximilian II, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1527–1576</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 31 July <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hugh-of-montgomery-2nd-earl-of-shrewsbury"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hugh-of-montgomery-2nd-earl-of-shrewsbury.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hugh of Montgomery, 2nd Earl of Shrewsbury</span><span class="tp">d. 1098</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ignatius-of-loyola"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ignatius-of-loyola.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ignatius of Loyola</span><span class="tp">1491–1556</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/luis-vicente-de-velasco"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/luis-vicente-de-velasco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Luis Vicente de Velasco</span><span class="tp">1711–1762</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/franz-liszt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/franz-liszt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Franz Liszt</span><span class="tp">1811–1886</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-younghusband"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-younghusband.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francis Younghusband</span><span class="tp">1863–1942</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/paul-henri-spaak"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/paul-henri-spaak.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Paul-Henri Spaak</span><span class="tp">1899–1972</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/omar-torrijos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/omar-torrijos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Omar Torrijos</span><span class="tp">1929–1981</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/baudouin-of-belgium"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/baudouin-of-belgium.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Baudouin of Belgium</span><span class="tp">1930–1993</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bao-dai.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bảo Đại</span><span class="tp">1913–1997</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
